{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00815",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.54,
      "end_seconds": 13.16,
      "duration_seconds": 12.62,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. Um, I've got this shake in my right hand, when I'm holding a cup of tea, and my daughter said I should see someone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.12,
      "end_seconds": 20.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Tell me about the shake. When does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.67,
      "end_seconds": 37.93,
      "duration_seconds": 15.26,
      "text": "When I pick up the cup, and lift it, it trembles. And when I write, my handwriting gets scrawly. It's not there when the hand is resting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.43,
      "end_seconds": 43.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.64,
      "end_seconds": 54.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "Oh, I'm not sure. A year ago? It could be longer. I forget these things."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.87,
      "end_seconds": 60.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Does it affect the other hand? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.57,
      "end_seconds": 70.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "A little, I think, in the left, but not as much. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.37,
      "end_seconds": 76.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Does alcohol make it better or worse? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.13,
      "end_seconds": 83.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "A glass of wine takes the edge off, actually. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.31,
      "end_seconds": 89.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Any slowness, stiffness, or trouble walking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.47,
      "end_seconds": 95.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "No, nothing like that. Walking's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.15,
      "end_seconds": 102.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "And caffeine, how much do you drink?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.53,
      "end_seconds": 109.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Four cups of tea a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.07,
      "end_seconds": 113.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.02,
      "end_seconds": 122.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Years ago, I came out in a rash on penicillin, so I've stayed away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.36,
      "end_seconds": 126.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Any other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.53,
      "end_seconds": 131.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "High blood pressure, and an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.77,
      "end_seconds": 137.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Does tremor run in the family? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.14,
      "end_seconds": 146.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "My father had it. We called it the family shake. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.7,
      "end_seconds": 156.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "That's useful. Let me examine you. Hold your arms out. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.63,
      "end_seconds": 177.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.21,
      "end_seconds": 195.13,
      "duration_seconds": 14.92,
      "text": "There's a fine tremor in both hands when you hold your arms out, worse on the right, and it increases when you reach for my finger. At rest it disappears."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.33,
      "end_seconds": 199.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Is it Parkinson's? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.38,
      "end_seconds": 215.98,
      "duration_seconds": 14.6,
      "text": "A rest tremor and slowness would be Parkinson's, and you don't have those. Let me check that. Walk across the room for me, and tap your fingers together. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.07,
      "end_seconds": 239.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.32,
      "end_seconds": 253.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.91,
      "text": "Your walking is normal, with good arm swing, and your finger-tapping is quick and even, with normal tone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.0,
      "end_seconds": 258.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "So it's not? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.1,
      "end_seconds": 274.11,
      "duration_seconds": 14.01,
      "text": "No, I'm not worried about Parkinson's. What you've got fits with a benign essential tremor, but I don't want to put a label on it yet. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.95,
      "end_seconds": 282.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "What would you like me to do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.74,
      "end_seconds": 290.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "Try cutting down the tea to two cups. Caffeine makes tremors worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.67,
      "end_seconds": 294.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Two cups. I'll try. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.73,
      "end_seconds": 301.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "And stress and tiredness too. It may settle. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.2,
      "end_seconds": 306.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Does it need tablets? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.42,
      "end_seconds": 318.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "Not unless it's affecting your life. If it is, there are tablets that help. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.12,
      "end_seconds": 324.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "It's the tea that bothers me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.61,
      "end_seconds": 334.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "Use a heavy cup, or a cup with two handles, and a straw if needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.82,
      "end_seconds": 338.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "That's a good idea. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.32,
      "end_seconds": 355.24,
      "duration_seconds": 14.92,
      "text": "If the tremor becomes much worse, you develop stiffness or slowness, or it starts at rest, come back and I'll refer you to a neurologist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.85,
      "end_seconds": 360.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "I will. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
